# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) to enable "Sign in with Google" in the AI panel.
#
# Create an OAuth client of type "Desktop app" in the Google Cloud console, enable the Generative
# Language API for the project, then paste the two values here. Leaving them unset is supported:
# the AI panel then says the browser login is not configured instead of failing inside Google's page.
#
# The secret is NOT confidential for a desktop app — it ships inside every binary you build, and
# Google's own docs say so. What protects the flow is PKCE, which `src/utils/aiAuth.ts` implements.
# Keeping the values out of the repo is about not handing strangers your project's API quota, not
# about hiding them from whoever runs the app.
#
# Rust reads the same client id from `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` at compile time (`src-tauri/src/oauth.rs`),
# used only as a fallback when the frontend passes none.

VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
